1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,549
Nine days ago, Maria asked about a blue
Toyota RAV4 Hybrid.

2
00:00:04,639 --> 00:00:08,058
The dealership last contacted her seven
days ago.

3
00:00:08,148 --> 00:00:10,700
Since then, that car has sold.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:15,569
There's still a silver RAV4 Hybrid
available at the same dealership.

5
00:00:15,659 --> 00:00:18,178
It's been sitting there for 74 days,

6
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:21,700
but nobody has followed up with Maria
about it.

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:26,700
Across 24 stores, there are over a
thousand leads that need attention.

8
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,680
A manager could work through those leads,

9
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:32,057
check which cars are still available,

10
00:00:32,147 --> 00:00:34,069
and look for alternatives.

11
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:36,489
But that means bringing together
information

12
00:00:36,579 --> 00:00:38,700
from several stores, every morning.

13
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,075
SalesDesk is your AI enterprise sales
analyst.

14
00:00:42,165 --> 00:00:46,700
It does that review overnight and prepares
the follow-ups for your team.

15
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:51,576
At 2 AM, it starts reviewing each store's
leads and inventory.

16
00:00:51,666 --> 00:00:55,700
Six stores run in parallel, in isolated
sandboxes on Vultr.

17
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,700
Let's look at Sandy.

18
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:02,988
SalesDesk reviews its 375 open leads and
flags 40 that need attention.

19
00:01:03,078 --> 00:01:06,803
Twenty-five have gone at least three days
without contact.

20
00:01:06,893 --> 00:01:10,188
Others are waiting on a car that has sold,

21
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:13,700
or have an appointment that needs
following up.

22
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:16,667
It then checks the available inventory:

23
00:01:16,757 --> 00:01:18,164
117 cars at Sandy

24
00:01:18,254 --> 00:01:21,700
and more than sixteen hundred at nearby
sister stores.

25
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:26,396
Each potential match is scored against
what the customer asked for,

26
00:01:26,486 --> 00:01:29,644
including the model, trim, budget and
mileage.

27
00:01:29,734 --> 00:01:33,700
Cars that have been in stock longer get
extra priority.

28
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:36,906
Qwen, running on Vultr Serverless
Inference,

29
00:01:36,996 --> 00:01:40,261
uses those checked results to write
Sandy's morning brief

30
00:01:40,351 --> 00:01:43,700
and three follow-up drafts for its
priority leads.

31
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,144
The recorded review finishes across all 24
stores

32
00:01:47,234 --> 00:01:49,700
in two minutes and seven seconds.

33
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,700
Here's Maria's result.

34
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:57,107
The silver RAV4 is the same model and trim
she originally asked about.

35
00:01:57,197 --> 00:02:02,700
It scores 98 out of 100, with the colour
difference shown in the breakdown.

36
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:05,982
The manager can see her original enquiry,

37
00:02:06,072 --> 00:02:08,173
when she was last contacted,

38
00:02:08,263 --> 00:02:12,700
and when the blue car sold, all in the
same view.

39
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:17,434
Below that is a draft message mentioning
the available silver RAV4

40
00:02:17,524 --> 00:02:20,809
and asking about her 2017 Honda CR-V
trade-in.

41
00:02:20,899 --> 00:02:23,997
The salesperson has the context and a
message

42
00:02:24,087 --> 00:02:26,700
ready to review before contacting her.

43
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:31,996
By the morning, Sandy's manager has a
ranked queue of 40 follow-ups.

44
00:02:32,086 --> 00:02:35,910
They can review individual drafts or
approve the queue together,

45
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,700
then download the tasks and drafts for
their salespeople.

46
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:45,884
Across the group, 1,007 at-risk leads have
been matched to a car in stock.

47
00:02:45,974 --> 00:02:50,738
The estimated gross associated with those
matches is about $3.4 million.

48
00:02:50,828 --> 00:02:55,700
Managers can use that view to decide where
their teams should focus.

49
00:02:56,200 --> 00:03:00,352
The scheduler and analysis jobs run on a
Vultr VM.

50
00:03:00,442 --> 00:03:03,088
Qwen runs on Vultr Serverless Inference,

51
00:03:03,178 --> 00:03:07,700
and its output is validated before it
reaches the approval queue.

52
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:12,432
SalesDesk gives your team a practical
starting point each morning:

53
00:03:12,522 --> 00:03:15,020
which customers to follow up with,

54
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:19,700
which cars to offer, and a draft they can
work from.

55
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,700
SalesDesk. Your AI enterprise sales
analyst.
